--
^warning: ignoring
--
Math functions with symbolic (non-constant) arguments return nondet
with range constraints (sin in [-1,1]) matching CBMC's C frontend.
Tests requiring exact values (sin(1.5708) ≈ 1.0) fail because the
solver can find counterexamples within the constrained range.
Fix would require a more precise math model or interval arithmetic.
Affects ~81 ESBMC tests.
